From b62039d86ded0dfdb8f08f8fa655ac07259c2d47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:14:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 24/25] mips: jz47xx: x2600: SPL: MSC0's clock gate open before
 the controller reset

ad5x_emmc_init() reset the SDHCI controller and only then opened its
clock gate (CLKGR0 bit 2, in emmc_set_clock()). From the eMMC that
works because the boot ROM read the SPL through MSC0 and left the gate
open. Started by the boot ROM over USB, nothing has opened it: the
reset and the register set-up after it would go to a gated controller.

Open the gate first, as the stock SPL's clk_init() does before its
msc_reset(). The chainload-test build does the same.
---
 arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl_emmc.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl_emmc.c b/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl_emmc.c
index fc639906..98ed2353 100644
--- a/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl_emmc.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl_emmc.c
@@ -211,6 +211,13 @@ int ad5x_emmc_init(void)
 	for (t = 0; (readl(CPM_MSC0CDR) & CDR_BUSY) && t < 10000; t++)
 		udelay(1);
 #endif
+	/*
+	 * The controller's clock before its first register access: the boot
+	 * ROM opens it only when it boots from the eMMC; started over USB
+	 * the gate may still be closed. The stock SPL's clk_init() opens it
+	 * before the reset too.
+	 */
+	clrbits_le32(CPM_CLKGR0, CLKGR0_MSC0);
 	if (emmc_reset(RESET_ALL))
 		return -EIO;
 	writel(~0U, MSC0 + SD_INT_ENABLE);	/* latch every status bit */
-- 
